In piping, a readable stream is connected to a writable stream, so data flows automatically from the source to the destination in chunks. 
This improves performance and memory usage, especially when handling large files.

Piping connects a readable stream to a writable stream automatically:
const readStream = fs.createReadStream('input.txt');
const writeStream = fs.createWriteStream('output.txt');
// Pipe data from read to write stream
readStream.pipe(writeStream);
writeStream.on('finish', () => {
console.log('File copied using streams');
});
